+    *   $s$ is the location of a sample point [S3].
+    *   $n$ is a sample normal [S3].
+    *   $T$ is the system matrix solved via singular value decomposition [S3].
 ### Parameters
-*   **$\theta$ (theta_sharp):** A parameter affecting the quality of remeshing, defined in Extended Marching Cubes (EMC) [KBSS01]. Larger values generate more triangles for regions with higher curvatures, while flat regions remain similar. Typical values tested: 0.7, 0.8, 0.9 [S3].
-
+*   **$\theta$ (theta_sharp):** A parameter affecting the quality of remeshing, defined in Extended Marching Cubes (EMC) [KBSS01]. Larger values generate more triangles for regions with higher curvatures, while flat regions remain similar [S3]. Typical values tested: 0.7, 0.8, 0.9 [S3].
 ### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Partial Implementations:** Some partial implementations may lack crucial features such as sharp edge preservation [S2].
-*   **Precision:** The SVD solution for sharp features requires careful handling of numerical stability [S3].
-*   **Ambiguity Resolution:** Incorrect resolution of face or internal ambiguities can lead to topological errors (holes or cracks) [S3].
-
